(READING ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.0 472.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(Reading a record from a file ) Tj
/F00 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 460.4 Tm
0.4840 Tw
(Let`s say you have a USMARC record in `file.dat' and you`d like to read in the record and print out its) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 448.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(title. ) Tj
/F10 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 436.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   1   ## Example R1 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 424.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   2 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 412.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   3   ## create a MARC::Batch object. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 400.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   4   use MARC::Batch; ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 388.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   5   my $batch = MARC::Batch\('USMARC', 'file.dat'\); ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 376.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   6 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 364.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   7   ## get a MARC record from the MARC::Batch object. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 352.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   8   ## the $record will be a MARC::Record object. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 340.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   9   my $record = $batch->next\(\); ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 328.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(  10 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 316.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(  11   ## print the title contained in the record. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 304.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(  12   print $record->title\(\),"\\n"; ) Tj
/F00 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 280.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(Using the distribution`s `t/camel.usmarc`, your result should be: ) Tj
/F10 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 268.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(  ActivePerl with ASP and ADO / Tobias Martinsson. ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 72.0 250.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(Iterating through a batch file ) Tj
/F00 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 238.4 Tm
0.6512 Tw
(Now imagine that `file.dat' actually contains multiple records and we want to print the title for each of) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 226.4 Tm
0.4845 Tw
(them. Our program doesn`t have to change very much at all: we just need to add a loop around our call) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 214.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(to ) Tj
/F10 10 Tf
0.0000 Tw
(next\(\)) Tj
/F00 10 Tf
0.0000 Tw
(. ) Tj
/F10 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 102.0 202.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   1   ## Example R2 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 190.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   2 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 178.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   3   ## create a MARC::Batch object. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 166.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   4   use MARC::Batch; ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 154.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   5   my $batch = MARC::Batch->new\('USMARC','file.dat'\); ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 142.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   6 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 130.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   7   while \(my $record = $batch->next\(\)\) \{ ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 118.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   8 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 106.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(   9     ## print the title contained in the record. ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 94.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(  10     print $record->title\(\),"\\n"; ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 82.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(  11 ) Tj
1 0 0 1 102.0 70.4 Tm
0.0000 Tw
(  12   \} ) Tj
/F21 10 Tf
